 *
 * KEY CONCEPT — Operator Overloading:
 *   Gives custom meaning to existing C++ operators (+, -, *, etc.)
 *   for user-defined class objects.
 *
 *   Syntax:
 *       ReturnType operator+(const ClassName& obj) {
 *           // define what + means for this class
 *       }
 *
 * IMPORTANT RULE in this lab:
 *   The task says operators are "swapped" for demonstration:
 *   operator+() → subtracts    operator-() → adds
 *   operator/() → multiplies   operator*() → divides
 */

